# Russian → Latin, ALA-LC (Library of Congress, Russian Romanization Table, 2012
# version), read from the LoC PDF; the Cyrillic codepoints are the PDF's own glyphs.
# Every letter has one romanization, so the table is the whole system. The tie in
# t͡s, i͡e, i͡u, i͡a is U+0361 COMBINING DOUBLE INVERTED BREVE after the first letter:
# the MARC 21 mapping since MARBI Proposal 2004-08 (approved 2004), which replaced
# the two ligature halves U+FE20/FE21 with it for new records. The table prints a
# capital's tie pair in capitals (Ц T͡S, Ю I͡U) and its digraphs in title case
# (Ж Zh). The soft and hard signs are U+02B9 ʹ and U+02BA ʺ. І Ѣ Ѳ Ѵ are the letters
